      "facts": "M.Sc. thesis (JKU Linz, supervised by Prof. Sepp Hochreiter, grade 1): conditional diffusion models used as generative classifiers for OOD detection. Class-conditional separation loss pushes the two class-conditioned noise predictions apart during training; at inference, the difference in reconstruction errors is compared with a calibrated threshold. On within-CIFAR-10 binary airplane-vs-rest (1,000 ID vs 9,000 OOD): 3-seed mean AUROC is 99.03% ± 0.07% at optimal lambda=0.02 vs 92.52% ± 11.07% at lambda=0.0 (+6.5 pp mean gain with far lower cross-seed variance). Single seed-42 within-CIFAR at lambda=0.02, K=100 reached 98.98% AUROC (4.7% FPR95, 99.87% AUPRC) vs seed-42 lambda=0.0 baseline 79.73% AUROC (60.2% FPR95). Qualifiers: binary single-ID-class benchmark, not comparable to multi-class CIFAR-10 OOD leaderboards or production accuracy.",
